00:34:55,100 --> 00:35:01,440
And by looking back to Leah and Rachel, the elders are essentially saying our God is faithful to keep his promises.

484
00:35:01,440 --> 00:35:05,620
That God has come through in the past and he's going to continue to come through.

485
00:35:05,620 --> 00:35:07,920
And now us on this side of the resurrection.

486
00:35:07,920 --> 00:35:14,760
How much more do we get to look back and see how God has been faithful to us in the midst of all of our brokenness and rebellion.

487
00:35:14,760 --> 00:35:17,640
That God continues to remain faithful to his promises.

488
00:35:17,640 --> 00:35:26,020
This radical act of sacrificial love that Boaz is participating in is not a blind act of faith that is not rooted in any reality.

489
00:35:26,020 --> 00:35:31,120
He can look back in the story of Israel and see how God is faithful to those who remain obedient to him.

490
00:35:31,120 --> 00:35:37,760
He says, yes, this redemption is coming a great sacrifice to me, but I can trust Yahweh who owns the land.

491
00:35:37,760 --> 00:35:38,760
Everything is his.

492
00:35:38,760 --> 00:35:40,900
I will not go hungry by obeying him.

493
00:35:40,900 --> 00:35:43,960
He comes back over and over.

494
00:35:43,960 --> 00:35:45,560
He comes through time and time again.

495
00:35:45,560 --> 00:35:49,500
And that is when we are invited to sacrificially lay down our life to follow Jesus.

496
00:35:49,500 --> 00:35:54,300
It's not a blind act of faith that is not rooted in the confidence of the past.

497
00:35:54,300 --> 00:35:57,480
We can look back to God's faithfulness in the past.

498
00:35:57,480 --> 00:36:01,940
Over and over and over again, he's been faithful in my life and in your life.

499
00:36:01,940 --> 00:36:07,040
And throughout human history, the God of the universe has been faithful to keep his promises.

500
00:36:07,040 --> 00:36:16,020
And so when he invites us to lay down our life and seek first his kingdom, it's an invitation that, yes, requires sacrifice, but we get far greater reward.

501
00:36:16,020 --> 00:36:18,500
It's a spiritual reward.

502
00:36:18,900 --> 00:36:29,860
It's not always an earthly reward, but if we're just doing earthly calculations, we're going to miss out on what God's invitation ultimately leads us to.

503
00:36:29,860 --> 00:36:35,500
The prayer concludes with the mention of Tamar and Judah, which we referenced last week.

504
00:36:35,500 --> 00:36:40,000
It's a testimony that God gets redemption done even when his people rebel against his invitation.

505
00:36:40,000 --> 00:36:45,400
It's a reminder that this new family is in the line of the promised Messiah.

506
00:36:45,400 --> 00:36:47,420
The Messiah would come through the line of Judah.

